  "problem": "A source card could declare Best for from topic tags alone. Missing essential facts could still look complete. Source-claim sentences might not resolve to evidence a reviewer can compare with a publisher passage. Readers could be forced through repeated caveats instead of purpose to variables to a tested access step. Editing sealed identity researcher-guidance.mjs would break WP7.",
  "resulting_behavior": "Source cards live in packages/enrichment/source-card.mjs. Purpose, coverage, grain, example variables, access steps, tested state, limits and citation are required. Documented use, reviewed recommendation and unsupported use are separate. Best for cannot be declared from topic tags alone. Missing essential facts produce an explicit incomplete status. HCRIS/PLACES examples have evidence-bound claims with publisher passages. Exact release/schema/example IDs and beginner/expert guides are attached. Unknowns stay compact. The web helper refuseBestForFromTopicTags enforces the same rule. Sealed packages/identity/src/researcher-guidance.mjs is unchanged (9805 bytes). Use-case fitness compares against context_only, not contextual.",
